 ('Which attitude toward natural disasters fits belief in destiny?', 'Taking precautions, helping one another and leaving the outcome to God', ['Blaming the victims', 'Rejecting scientific precaution', 'Taking no precautions'], 'Belief in destiny calls for taking precautions and helping each other.', 'Destiny and decree'),
 ('To what extent do a person’s good or bad actions belong to them?', 'To the extent of choices within their will and power', ['Not at all', 'Only by chance', 'To the extent of everyone else’s choices'], 'A person is responsible for conduct within their will and power.', 'Destiny and decree'),
 ('What does it mean that human will is limited?', 'A person cannot control everything but chooses within their power', ['A person decides in God’s place', 'A person is not responsible for anything', 'A person knows the future completely'], 'A person does not control everything, but chooses within their power and is responsible.', 'Destiny and decree'),
 ('What error does excessive fatalism about destiny lead to?', 'Neglecting responsibility and precaution', ['Increasing work and effort', 'Multiplying good', 'Upholding what is right'], 'Excessive fatalism leads to neglecting responsibility and precaution.', 'Destiny and decree'),
