 ('According to al-Baqara 286, what does God not burden a person with?', 'More than they can bear', ['Any responsibility', 'Prayer', 'Zakat'], 'Al-Baqara 286 says: “God does not burden a soul beyond its capacity.”', 'Destiny and decree'),
 ('What did ‘Umar say to those who objected to turning back from Syria upon learning of the plague?', 'We flee from God’s decree to God’s decree', ['There is no escape from fate, so we go on', 'The plague is not destiny', 'God will not protect us'], '‘Umar, turning back as a precaution, said “We flee from God’s decree to God’s decree” (Bukhari, Muslim).', 'Destiny and decree'),
 ('According to the hadith of Ibn Mas‘ud, what does the angel write for the child in the womb?', 'His provision, his term, his deeds and whether he will be happy or wretched', ['Only his name', 'Only his height', 'Nothing'], 'According to the hadith, the angel writes the child’s provision, term, deeds and whether he will be fortunate or wretched (Bukhari, Muslim).', 'Destiny and decree'),
 ('What path has Ahl al-Sunna taken on destiny?', 'A middle path between determinism and human absolute creation', ['Only determinism', 'Only human will', 'Never discussing destiny'], 'Ahl al-Sunna takes a middle path (kasb) between jabriyya and qadariyya.', 'Destiny and decree'),
